  "reviewed_interpretation": "On fresh diagnostic seeds, nonstationary weak starts split into 13 speech and 10 noise events. All 10 noise weak starts were local-admissible, guard-inactive and had no upstream blend; all 7 weak starts with blend_applied were speech. Stationary weak starts were 15 speech and 1 noise and all 16 used blend. The existing guard itself is not a useful positive admission rule: it was inactive for all nonstationary weak starts and active only for the single stationary noise weak start. The evidence supports a separately frozen state-only test requiring an actual upstream blend to start weak activity, but I019 selects no candidate and adds no threshold.",
